lished suppression excess", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "The published H1->H2 suppression excess (0.408) exceeds what regression to the mean and selection on the H2 drop produce under no true change.", "observed_result": "No log saved; analytic_bias.py print string cites 'observed 0.408, simulation 0.440' for E[excess|H0].", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Null simulation with no true change gives excess ~0.440 vs observed 0.408 (numbers quoted in analytic_bias.py print text; no log).", "observed_sample_and_power": "1,136 caliper pairs"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:insufficient_exposure"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:EXPOSURE_SPARSITY"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:RTM_SELECTION"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-052", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-052: Play-type replacement similarity vs absorb/cascade", "score": 0.217, "reached_via": ["request matches DS:Player_absence_spells (0.35); FAM:SF-CHT-052 auto_uses_dataset DS:Player_absence_spells", "request matches RQC:RQC-139 (0.16); FAM:SF-CHT-052 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-139"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Play-type replacement similarity vs absorb/cascade", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "Having a similar-profile teammate separates absorption from cascade when a player sits.", "observed_result": "mean sim ABSORBED +0.863 vs CASCADE +0.848; Spearman(sim, -gap)=-0.19 (wrong-signed). Embiid 23-24 cascades with Reed sim 0.94.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Similarity does not separate absorption from cascade; almost always findable.", "observed_sample_and_power": "NOT_RECORDED", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null", "observed_failure_type": "B_powered_null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-005"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-CHT-032"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-CHT-086"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-088", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-088: Offensive-identity resilience: connector absence vs usage-matched others", "score": 0.212, "reached_via": ["request matches DS:Player_absence_spells (0.35); FAM:SF-APPS-088 auto_uses_dataset DS:Player_absence_spells", "request matches RQC:RQC-013 (0.22); FAM:SF-APPS-088 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-013"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Offensive-identity resilience: connector absence vs usage-matched others", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "Connector absence displaces team offensive identity (D_A) more than usage-matched non-organizer absence.", "observed_result": "Unmatched conn vs role D_A 0.2020 vs 0.1021, t=5.97 p=2.87e-08. Usage-matched vs role: paired dD_A +0.1151, P(conn>ctrl)=81.2%, t=6.35 p=7.35e-09 n=96. Vs terminal: +0.0777 t=2.37 p=0.0261 n=25.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "D_positive (no failure: positive result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Usage-matched connector vs role occupant identity break is large and significant (n=96). Licensed comparison excludes organizers.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=96 matched pairs vs role; n=25 vs terminal; 908 player-seasons"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-PAP-014"}]}], "n_results": 4}

